# Copy to .env and fill in — docker-compose.yml loads this automatically
# and forwards ANTHROPIC_API_KEY into the backend container.
# Generation (Selection, Rewrite, Cover Letter drafting, RAL Range
# estimation) calls the Claude API directly, per ADR-0005.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional Claude model overrides (ADR-0025). Each kind of Claude call runs
# on a built-in default model chosen for that kind of work — see the docs site's
# Configuration page (site/src/content/docs/configuration.md). Leave these unset (or empty) to keep
# the defaults. A per-call-site variable wins over SUMISURA_MODEL_DEFAULT,
# which in turn wins over the built-in default. Values are passed to the API
# unchanged; a model missing from backend/internal/claude/pricing.go still
# works but logs a warning and estimates its cost at $0.
#
# SUMISURA_MODEL_DEFAULT=
# SUMISURA_MODEL_SELECTION_REWRITE=claude-opus-5
# SUMISURA_MODEL_SELECTION_PREVIEW=
# SUMISURA_MODEL_COVER_LETTER=
# SUMISURA_MODEL_RAL_RESEARCH=
# SUMISURA_MODEL_RAL_EXTRACTION=
# SUMISURA_MODEL_APPLICATION_METHOD_INFERENCE=
# SUMISURA_MODEL_CONTACT_RESEARCH=
# SUMISURA_MODEL_CONTACT_EXTRACTION=

# Optional LAN-reachable mode (issue #57). Leave both unset for the default,
# unchanged behavior: localhost-only, no auth. To make the app reachable
# from other devices on your LAN, set both of these and start with
# `docker compose --profile lan up`:
#
# BIND_ADDR=0.0.0.0
# LAN_AUTH_TOKEN=<a long random string>
#
# Once LAN_AUTH_TOKEN is set, every /api/* request needs access: the web app
# asks for the token once per device and keeps an HttpOnly cookie derived
# from it; non-browser clients (the extension, an iOS Shortcut) send it in
# the X-Sumisura-Token header. Changing the token signs every device out.
# This is a single static shared secret, not a login system, and LAN mode
# itself has no TLS — see the docs site's "LAN-reachable mode" page for the
# tradeoffs before enabling this on an untrusted network.
